+\paragraph{Team responsibilities.}
+\textbf{Zhang Zhichao} will cover molecular-generation literature, research-question
+formulation, and overall study design; adapt ChemGPT loading, sampling, and
+decoding interfaces for integration with the RL framework; and coordinate the
+proposal's background, motivation, and overall narrative in the final report.
+
+\textbf{Liao Yang} will develop the GuacaMol task, property-scoring, and reward
+interfaces; implement evaluation budgets, duplicate-molecule caching, and the
+frozen-model baseline; organize comparison runs; and carry out metric
+verification, result analysis, figures, and experimental reporting.
+
+\textbf{Han Gaofei} will focus on RL-method design and implementation, including
+REINFORCE, the variance-reduction baseline, the frozen reference policy, and KL
+regularization; verify policy updates, gradient correctness, and training
+stability; develop training configurations; and write the methods section and
+interpret the optimization behavior.
+
+\paragraph{Joint work and deliverables.}
+All three members will jointly finalize experiments, cross-check code and
+results, discuss conclusions, integrate the report, prepare the presentation,
+and participate in Q\&A. Deliverables are versioned code and configurations,
+complete generation/scoring logs, per-seed metrics, necessary checkpoints,
+and a reproducible final report. Negative results and quality--diversity
+trade-offs will be retained. The schedule is summarized in Table~\ref{tab:schedule}.
 
